  "critique": {
    "axis": "clarity",
    "evidence": "The headline, one-sentence instruction, prominent controls, and single “Launch Event” CTA make the immediate task understandable across all viewports. The side-by-side ALLOW/BLOCK result and fused-risk explanation clearly communicate the intended comparison. However, the screen does not identify which control was changed, distinguish pre-launch placeholder results from returned results, or visibly tie the displayed outcome to the selected inputs. On mobile, the global header hides Composer off-screen and relies on a vague “SWIPE →” cue.",
    "fix": "Add an explicit initial/result state: hide or label results as awaiting launch, then show “Result for these inputs” with a compact summary of the submitted values and highlight the changed control. In the mobile header, expose the current section or provide a clear navigation affordance.",
